# Safe Modification Zones

## Green Zone (Full Autonomy)
- All files in `Assets/scripts/Debuggers/`
- `Assets/scripts/UI/` (except core GameUI.cs)
- ScriptableObject assets in `Assets/data/`
- Wave/Stage data files
- Test files in `Assets/scripts/Testing/`
- Debug panels and visualization

## Yellow Zone (Conditional Autonomy)
Safe to Modify:
- Adding new private methods to existing managers
- Optimizing existing methods
- Adding debug features
- Improving error handling
- Adding validation

Requires Approval:
- Changing public API
- Modifying interfaces
- Altering communication patterns
- Changing initialization

## Red Zone (No Autonomy - Requires Approval)
- `Assets/scripts/Utils/Enumerations.cs`
- Unity lifecycle methods (Awake, Start, Update)
- Singleton implementations
- Manager communication patterns
- GridManager.cs (core methods)
- WaveManager.cs (wave progression)
- PlayerActionManager.cs (input handling)
- StageManager.cs (progression logic)
- PlayerManager.cs (core player logic)
